cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, cite this release. For the investigation findings, cite the related preprint listed below."
title: "UNK_DeadDrop Companion"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Krasnjanski
    given-names: Ilja
    affiliation: Independent researcher
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-1039-5930"
version: 2.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/KrasForge/unk-deaddrop-companion"
abstract: "Parse-only JavaScript AST scanning and 33 experimental YARA rules in 28 files for defensive analysis of developer-targeting lures. Every rule matched retained case artifacts in a read-only replay; a small local software baseline produced no hits. Sigma event rules are omitted because authentic endpoint logs were unavailable for replay. Includes inert boundary tests and documents operational limits."
keywords:
  - malware analysis
  - detection engineering
  - static analysis
  - YARA
references:
  - type: preprint
    authors:
      - family-names: Krasnjanski
        given-names: Ilja
    title: "UNK_DeadDrop: An Artifact-Based Study of Recruitment Malware, Credential Collection, and Operator Infrastructure"
    year: 2026
    doi: "10.5281/zenodo.23696198"
    url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23696198"
